# Copy to ~/.config/linux-cleaner/env (see RUNBOOK.md systemd section).
# Safe-tier defaults for systemd EnvironmentFile=-
# linux-cleaner-clean.service passes only --clean --force, so LINUX_CLEANER_TRASH
# and LINUX_CLEANER_RISK in this file apply to the timer.
LINUX_CLEANER_FORCE=1
# Enabling LINUX_CLEANER_TRASH makes the daily timer quarantine instead of delete
# (predefined action:* rows still delete; see README).
# Set LINUX_CLEANER_TRASH_KEEP_DAYS (or enable linux-cleaner-retention.timer) to
# purge old quarantine sessions automatically.
# LINUX_CLEANER_TRASH=1
# LINUX_CLEANER_TRASH_KEEP_DAYS=30
LINUX_CLEANER_RISK=safe
# Optional bounded contention wait; literal decimal 0..2147483647 seconds.
# Unset/empty/0 fails fast; positive requires flock. CLI --lock-wait overrides.
# LINUX_CLEANER_LOCK_WAIT=30
# Raising LINUX_CLEANER_RISK above safe makes the unattended deletion of medium
# targets (for example package caches) irreversible. C++ build rows are safe.
# LINUX_CLEANER_QUIET=1
# LINUX_CLEANER_DEBUG=1
# Send a desktop notification summarizing the cleanup result, or a critical notice when the run stops early with an error (requires notify-send).
# LINUX_CLEANER_NOTIFY=1
# Stop after the first failed cleanup target and skip inline retention.
# LINUX_CLEANER_FAIL_FAST=1
# Write Prometheus node_exporter textfile metrics at every non-dry-run cleanup exit
# (except failures before the config loads, such as a missing config file)
# (literal absolute path, replaced atomically). The directory must be
# writable by your user, since this unit runs unprivileged; point the textfile
# collector at it.
# LINUX_CLEANER_METRICS_FILE=/home/USER/.local/share/node_exporter/linux_cleaner.prom
# Optional env-only preview gauges for monitor dry runs (text or JSON): timestamp,
# planned reclaimable bytes, and would-skip (1 for threshold/nothing-to-clean skips).
# Uses the same atomic write and path checks: literal absolute path without LF,
# existing writable directory, no symlinked file or parent. Use a different path
# from LINUX_CLEANER_METRICS_FILE; equality warns and skips preview export.
# Unset/empty writes nothing. Mutating cleanup and all non-cleanup modes ignore it.
# Invalid paths and write errors warn without failing the dry run.
# LINUX_CLEANER_PREVIEW_METRICS_FILE=/home/USER/.local/share/node_exporter/linux_cleaner_preview.prom
# Use an absolute config path here: EnvironmentFile does not expand $HOME,
# and the cleaner uses LINUX_CLEANER_CONFIG literally. Unset uses normal discovery.
# LINUX_CLEANER_CONFIG=/absolute/path/to/cleaner.conf
# LINUX_CLEANER_ONLY_TARGET=NPM
# LINUX_CLEANER_EXCLUDE_TARGET=Chromium
# Select one existing project using a literal absolute path (no $HOME/tilde/globs).
# CLI --only-path overrides; unset/empty means no scope. Excludes action:* rows.
# Do not combine with LINUX_CLEANER_TRASH_KEEP_DAYS; use the retention timer instead.
# LINUX_CLEANER_ONLY_PATH="/absolute/project path"
# Skip one existing directory (and every target at, below, or containing it); literal
# absolute path. CLI --exclude-path overrides; unset/empty means no exclusion.
# LINUX_CLEANER_EXCLUDE_PATH="/absolute/project path"
# Skip the daily cleanup when the planned reclaimable total is below this size.
# LINUX_CLEANER_MIN_RECLAIM=500M
# Skip the daily cleanup when the home filesystem already has at least this much free.
# LINUX_CLEANER_MIN_FREE=10G
# Raise every ordinary target's age threshold to at least this many days; skips action:* rows.
# LINUX_CLEANER_MIN_AGE=14
# Stop each action:* command (paccache, nix-store --gc, ...) after this many seconds
# and count it failed, so later targets, retention and the report still run.
# LINUX_CLEANER_ACTION_TIMEOUT=1800
# Operation log path under $HOME; the cleaner expands a leading $HOME or ~ itself
# (systemd does not).
# LINUX_CLEANER_LOG=/home/USER/.cache/linux-cleaner/ops.log
# LINUX_CLEANER_JSON is for dry-run, inventory and --report only; leave it unset for
# the cleanup service. Use linux-cleaner-monitor.service for scheduled JSON previews.
# Comma-separated patterns never cleaned inside any target.
# LINUX_CLEANER_EXCLUDE=.git,*.log
# LINUX_CLEANER_ALLOW_OUTSIDE_HOME is deprecated and ignored. Targets outside
# HOME are always allowed. Package-cache rows stay medium risk, so they still
# need LINUX_CLEANER_RISK=medium; under RISK=safe they are not selected.
# Never schedule by default — danger-tier bypass.
# LINUX_CLEANER_YES_DANGER=1
# Retention age lives in linux-cleaner-retention.service (older-than:30). To change it
# so a reinstall keeps it, run `systemctl --user edit linux-cleaner-retention.service`
# and add, under [Service], an empty ExecStart= that clears the shipped command, then yours:
#   ExecStart=
#   ExecStart=/usr/bin/env cleaner --purge-sessions older-than:DAYS --force --lock-wait 3600
